Hmm. But wait, is the loan payment something he had to pay from the sale proceeds? Like, when you sell a house, you usually have to pay off any remaining mortgage. So yes, the $250,000 would come out of the proceeds. So that all seems correct. The transfer fees and brokerage fees are also costs associated with the sale. So subtracting them all makes sense.

So I think the answer is 118,000. Let me check once again.

Total fees: 3% + 5% = 8% of 400,000. 8% is 0.08 * 400,000 = 32,000. Then minus the loan of 250k. 32k + 250k = 282k. 400k - 282k = 118k. Yep, same answer. So I think that's correct.
